menu "embpet proto"

    config EMBPET_PROTO_STRESS
        bool "Frame writer stress test (never enable in production)"
        default n
        help
            Two tasks each emit 1000 events while ESP_LOGW spams, three seconds
            after boot. Check on the host with
            tools/embpet_cli.py --check-frames SEC --reset.

    config EMBPET_CONSOLE_SOAK
        bool "Console soak generator (never enable in production)"
        default n
        help
            A task emits a "soak" event and a WARN log line every 100 ms and
            reports the longest event write, log write and loop period it has
            seen since uptime 15 s, so a host can show the firmware kept running
            while the port was closed. Host side: tools/console_test.py soak.

    config EMBPET_BOOT_TRACE
        bool "Boot stall trace (never enable in production)"
        default n
        depends on EMBPET_CONSOLE_SOAK && FREERTOS_GENERATE_RUN_TIME_STATS
        help
            Records late wake-ups of a priority-5 and a priority-24 task, late
            esp_timer callbacks, per-task CPU, and the timing of PHY
            calibration, the WPA PMK derivation, flash erase/write, TLS
            handshakes and Wi-Fi events until uptime 20 s; `trace` returns
            the records (embpet-s2j.5, tools/boot_trace.py).

    config EMBPET_CONSOLE_PROBE
        bool "Console CPU probe commands (never enable in production)"
        default n
        depends on FREERTOS_GENERATE_RUN_TIME_STATS
        help
            Adds `probe cpu` (run-time counters of the console and idle tasks,
            in us) and `probe nop` (an empty ok res), so a host can measure
            console CPU per command (tools/console_cpu.py), and `probe sleep
            <ms>` / `probe echo <text>` / `probe rxoff` to test input that
            arrives while a command blocks and the RX flow control
            (tools/console_test.py pipeline).

endmenu
